Malaria Report 2012</source><year>2012</year><publisher-name>Geneva: World Health Organization</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>van Eijk</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Alegana</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirui</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gething</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>ter Kuile</surname><given-names>FO</given-names></name><name><surname>Snow</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><article-title>Coverage of malaria protection in pregnant women in sub-Saharan Africa: a synthesis and analysis of national survey data</article-title><source>Lancet Infect Dis</source><year>2011</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>190</fpage><lpage>207</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1473-3099(10)70295-4</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21273130</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Sevene</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonz&#x000e1;lez</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Men&#x000e9;ndez</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><article-title>Current knowledge and challenges of antimalarial drugs for treatment and prevention in pregnancy</article-title><source>Expert Opin Pharmacother</source><year>2010</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>1277</fpage><lpage>1293</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1517/14656561003733599</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">20408744</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>Malaria in Pregnancy Consortium</article-title><comment>[<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.mip-consortium.org/">http://www.mip-consortium.org/</ext-link>]</comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Pell</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Straus</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Andrew</surname><given-names>EVW</given-names></name><name><surname>Menaca</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pool</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><article-title>Social and cultural factors affecting uptake of interventions for malaria in pregnancy in Africa: a systematic review of the qualitative research</article-title><source>PLoS One</source><year>2011</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>e22452</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0022452</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21799859</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Menaca</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pell</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Manda</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Chatio</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Afrah</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Were</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodgson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ouma</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalilani</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Tagbor</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Pool</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><article-title>Local illness concepts and their relevance for the prevention and control of malaria during pregnancy in Ghana, Kenya and Malawi: findings from a comparative qualitative study</article-title><source>Malar J</source><year>2013</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>257</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1475-2875-12-257</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">23876079</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Pell</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Me&#x000f1;aca</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Were</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Afrah</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chatio</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Manda-Taylor</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamel</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodgson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tagbor</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalilani</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><article-title>Factors Affecting antenatal care attendance: results from qualitative studies in Ghana, Kenya and Malawi</article-title><source>PLoS One</source><year>2013</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>e53747</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0053747</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">23335973</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><collab>Ghana Statistical Service</collab><source>Guidelines for the treatment of malaria, 2010</source><year>2010</year><publisher-name>Geneva, Switzerland: World Health Organization</publisher-name><fpage>194</fpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Bardaj&#x000ed;</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sigauque</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruni</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Romagosa</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mabunda</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mandomando</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Aponte</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sevene</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Alonso</surname><given-